{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>Behold</b> — when the day comes that all the nations gather against Jerusalem, after the death of the pierced one mentioned above." "<b>And the spoil</b> — with Jerusalem he speaks, and the nation, that the spoil of the enemy will be divided. If so, why after it: \"and half the city shall go out into exile\"? And further, ונשסו [and the houses shall be stripped] — from the root of doubling, like ונמקו כל צבא השמים (and all the host of heaven shall melt away); like נסבו from סבב."], :book :zechariah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {1 "The phrase ונשסו הבתים appears in the verse; Ibn Ezra parses it as a doubling/biliteral root analogous to נמק and נסב. His grammatical terminology here (מפעלי הכפל) is elliptical; rendered literally as 'of doubling.' The clause 'והאומה כי' is textually awkward but translated as read."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Zecharia -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/zecharya"] ["1" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=25&perek=5&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:47:04.288526390Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}